message: "If you use this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Compression Physics: A Domain-Normalized Efficiency Index (Generalized Efficiency Coefficient, GEC)"
version: "2.0.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.17785197"
date-released: "2025-12-01"

authors:
  - family-names: Brooks
    given-names: Mycal
    orcid: "0009-0006-7513-8532"  

repository-code: "https://github.com/ToweraiDev/compression-physics-reproducibility"
abstract: >
  This work introduces the Generalized Efficiency Coefficient (GEC), a domain-normalized 
  measure of system efficiency that unifies metrics across physics, engineering, and 
  information systems. It defines a universal framework—“Compression Physics”—for 
  evaluating how closely a process approaches its theoretical or empirical efficiency bound.
